plicit facts, explain why evidence supports or weakens candidate's case, and be consistent with metadata vote.\n\nWe are Agent 3. Our current vote is Candidate B (as per shared mental model). We need to either keep that or change. We should consider D's traits. We have facts: D responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as a loner, hot temper, know-it-all. Also D is considered moody and loner, which are concerns for crew cooperation. B is pretentious and sometimes wrong tone. We need to argue.\n\nWe can argue that while D's problem solving and responsibility are strong, the interpersonal issues (hot temper, moody, loner) are more severe for crew cooperation than B's pretentiousness and tone issues. Also B's reliability and stress handling are proven. So we keep B.\n\nWe can also ask for any missing info about D's crew cooperation, but we may not need to ask tool. We have no direct evidence of D's crew cooperation, but we have concerns. So we can argue that without evidence of good crew cooperation, D remains riskier.\n\nThus we will state we still recommend Candidate B, because B's reliability, stress resilience, technical competence outweigh the interpersonal concerns, and D's interpersonal concerns are more significant.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: mention Agent 1's points, and also earlier contributions about B and C.\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: B very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills; D solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, but hot temper, moody, loner.\n\nWe need to explain why B remains best.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate B."}
